# Controller vs service

- Controllers only map HTTP and **delegate**. No payload building, DB, Kafka, Redis, or reason→action rules in a controller.
- Map exceptions to HTTP in `exception/` (`@RestControllerAdvice`), not in the controller method.
- All business logic lives in `service/` subpackages (`service/webhook`, `service/ingest`, `service/plan`), or small helpers those services call.

# Service size

- Each class under `service/` must stay **under 200 lines**. Put new work in the matching subfolder (`webhook`, `ingest`, `plan`) instead of growing one file.
- Do not put HTTP `ResponseEntity` construction in a service. Throw a typed exception; let the controller/advice choose the status.

```java
// BAD — logic in the controller
@RestController
class WebhookSimulateController {
  SimulatedFailureResult run() { ingest.consume(buildJson()); }
}

// GOOD — controller delegates
@RestController
class WebhookSimulateController {
  SimulatedFailureResult simulateOne(@PathVariable String slug) {
    return simulateService.simulateOne(slug);
  }
}
```
